{
 "title": "Was Stalin Necessary? Counterfactual Evidence on Soviet Growth",
 "hypothesis": "The post-1928 Russian-core growth path exceeds ordinary admissible statistical and historically disciplined counterfactuals including a bootstrap recovery-gap NEP alternative",
 "data_sources": [
  "Global Macro Database RUS GDP and GDP per capita",
  "Maddison Project Database 2023 RUS and SUN GDP per capita",
  "CIA/RAND Soviet national accounts GNP 1928-1954",
  "Markevich-Harrison 1913-1928 bridge",
  "COW / Federico-Tena / JST / Barro-Lee auxiliary donor diagnostics"
 ],
 "sample": "Russian-core series labelled RUS and broader Soviet territorial aggregate labelled SUN. Primary statistical inference on GMD RUS and Maddison RUS/SUN. Donor panel of 28 countries for principal GMD RUS SCM through 1940. Effective spatial placebo set 8 donors. Historical analogues and donor percentile frontiers are not treated as country substitutes.",
 "period_start": "1900",
 "period_end": "1940",
 "method": [
  "1. Construct long-run log output and log output per capita from GMD and Maddison Project. Bridge 1913-1928 from Markevich-Harrison. Triangulation from CIA/RAND GNP and end-use accounts.",
  "2. Normalize every observed and counterfactual trajectory to 1928=100: if first observed log level is y_1929 and first annual log growth is g_1929 then y_1928 = y_1929 - g_1929 and index_t = 100*exp(y_t - y_1928). Principal endpoint 1938; sensitivity endpoints 1933,1934,1936,1940. 1939-1940 treated as mobilisation sensitivity.",
  "3. Estimate statistical counterfactuals with distinct failure modes: SCM convex nonnegative weights summing to one, NNLS normalized, Augmented SCM ridge bias correction, Synthetic Difference-in-Differences unit and time weights, Generalized Synthetic Control interactive fixed effects via donor PCA/factor ridge, Matrix Completion low-rank SVD/nuclear-norm imputation, Conformal trajectory bands residual-based.",
  "4. Estimate predictive benchmarks for comparison only: Ridge synthetic, Bayesian ridge, Elastic net sparse, Huber robust synthetic, PLS latent synthetic, Random forest, Extra trees, Gradient boosting, kNN synthetic flagged overfit risk, Super learner ensemble of valid non-causal predictive models.",
  "5. Estimate NEP alternative as bootstrap recovery-gap process. Estimate prewar log-linear trend from Russian 1900-1913. Define annual recovery gap G_t = log Y_potential_t - log Y_observed_t. Estimate annual persistence rho = G_t / G_{t-1} from 1921-1928 gap ratios AR(1)-style. Residual bootstrap resamples uncertainty in prewar trend and gap-closure ratios. For each draw log Y_NEP_t = log Y_potential_t - G_1928 * rho^(t-1928). Median and 5th/95th percentiles reported. Mechanical constant extrapolation of 1922-1928 recovery rate retained only as stress archive excluded from primary admissible frontier ASCF. NEP slow reversion, fast reversion, capped at high donor percentile also in archive.",
  "6. Construct frontiers: Donor p75 admissible frontier, Donor p90 stress hostile upper bound. Scenario Tsarist mean trend, Japan-like, Turkey-like, Italy-like historical analogues kept separate and donor percentile labelled adversarial ex post annual envelope not feasible trajectory. Population denominator recomputed with alternative demographic assumptions as stress.",
  "7. Diagnostics: pre-treatment RMSE, pre-treatment correlation, conformal band crossing, endpoint sensitivity, model-family distribution of premiums. Pre-RMSE ranking used to weight matrix completion over weak pre-fit estimators.",
  "8. Donor perturbation: leave-one-donor-out for each influential donor and random 75 percent donor subpools; report cumulative premium percent and annualised premium percent.",
  "9. Falsification: spatial placebos reassign treatment to donors with same estimator exact two-sided rank p = 1/(n_placebos+1). Post/pre RMSPE ratio complementary diagnostic. Fake treatment origins assigned in 1905 evaluated 1917 horizon 12, 1913 evaluated 1925 horizon 12, 1921 evaluated 1928 horizon 7, 1924 evaluated 1928 horizon 4, 1926 evaluated 1928 horizon 2. Recovery placebos for post-collapse episodes. Donor-pool perturbations; endpoint sensitivity.",
  "10. Independent national-account triangulation: CIA/RAND average annual Soviet GNP growth for 1928-37, 1937-40, 1928-54 two estimates A and B; end-use composition consumption/investment/military share by 1940."
 ],
